TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The whole song can be played with just (G), (C), and (A).  But the (CaddG) in the intro and the (Gadd) in the outro are easy to play.  (CaddG) is just (C) with your pinky added to the 1st string/3rd fret.  In the intro it comes immediately before the first word in the line and then you move quickly on to the (G).}

TIP:  The first two verses are the same, the first is the sung acapella by a choir followed by a short guitar and horn interlude and then Mick's first verse.}
  

